# StatsManager — Statistics & Playtime Tracking
# Files: src/coordinator/StatsManager.h, StatsManager.cpp

## PURPOSE
Persists game start counts, puck usage stats, and total playtime to NVS + LittleFS.

## GAME STARTS
- gameStarts[30] array, indices 1-29 used
- Stored in NVS Preferences namespace "pr_stats", keys "g1" to "g29"
- addGameStart(id), getGameStarts(id)

## PUCK STATS
- Per-puck clicks and minutes stored in NVS
- Key format: last 6 hex chars of MAC + "_c" (clicks) or "_t" (time)
- getPuckClicks(mac), getPuckTime(mac)
- PuckNetwork tracks totalClicks/totalMinutes in PuckInfo struct

## PLAYTIME TRACKING (License System)
- Dual storage: NVS ("pr_hw" namespace, keys "_ct"/"_cv") + LittleFS ("/._sys.dat")
- Integrity: XOR checksum with PT_MAGIC (0xA7C3E1B9)
- On boot: loads from both, takes HIGHER value (tamper protection)
- startPlaytime(): records session start
- stopPlaytime(): adds elapsed minutes, saves to both stores
- getTotalPlaytimeMinutes(): includes running session
- Crash protection: saveAll() persists running session periodically

## saveAll()
- Called periodically from PuckNetwork (every 10 minutes)
- Saves game starts + puck stats to NVS
- Saves playtime to both NVS and LittleFS
